; InstallDayna - non-interactive install of the patched scsidayna.device
; (SANA-II DaynaPort driver) PLUS the Roadshow network configuration.
;
; Rewritten 2026-08-07 after the first A500 install: the old version only
; copied the driver+prefs and left the TCP-stack side ("configure it
; yourself") - which is exactly the part that made it "not really work".
; This version writes everything the working A500 setup needed:
;   DEVS:Networks/scsidayna.device
;   ENVARC:scsidayna.prefs + ENV: copy   (AUTOCONNECT=1 + WiFi creds)
;   DEVS:NetInterfaces/scsidayna         (static IP interface)
;   DEVS:Internet/Routes                 (default gateway)
;   DEVS:Internet/name_resolution        (DNS)
; Existing config files are NOT overwritten (so re-running is safe on an
; already-tuned machine) - it says "kept existing" instead.
;
; Defaults below are one example LAN (a static 192.168.50.36). Edit for your own.
; For an interactive walkthrough use the full "Install" script instead.
;
; Run from the drawer containing scsidayna.device and scsidayna.prefs:
;   Execute InstallDayna

If NOT EXISTS DEVS:Networks
  MakeDir DEVS:Networks
EndIf
Copy scsidayna.device DEVS:Networks/ CLONE QUIET
Echo "Installed DEVS:Networks/scsidayna.device"
If EXISTS daynawifi
  Copy daynawifi C: CLONE QUIET
  Protect C:daynawifi +e
  Echo "Installed C:daynawifi (the adapter's Wi-Fi: status, REJOIN, SCAN)"
EndIf

If EXISTS ENVARC:scsidayna.prefs
  Echo "kept existing ENVARC:scsidayna.prefs"
Else
  Copy scsidayna.prefs ENVARC:scsidayna.prefs CLONE QUIET
  Echo "Installed ENVARC:scsidayna.prefs (check SSID/KEY inside!)"
EndIf
Copy ENVARC:scsidayna.prefs ENV:scsidayna.prefs CLONE QUIET

If NOT EXISTS DEVS:NetInterfaces
  MakeDir DEVS:NetInterfaces
EndIf
If EXISTS DEVS:NetInterfaces/scsidayna
  Echo "kept existing DEVS:NetInterfaces/scsidayna"
Else
  Echo >DEVS:NetInterfaces/scsidayna "device=scsidayna.device"
  Echo >>DEVS:NetInterfaces/scsidayna "address=192.168.50.36"
  Echo >>DEVS:NetInterfaces/scsidayna "netmask=255.255.255.0"
  Echo "Wrote DEVS:NetInterfaces/scsidayna (static 192.168.50.36)"
EndIf

If NOT EXISTS DEVS:Internet
  MakeDir DEVS:Internet
EndIf
If EXISTS DEVS:Internet/Routes
  Echo "kept existing DEVS:Internet/Routes"
Else
  Echo >DEVS:Internet/Routes "default 192.168.50.1"
  Echo "Wrote DEVS:Internet/Routes (gateway 192.168.50.1)"
EndIf
If EXISTS DEVS:Internet/name_resolution
  Echo "kept existing DEVS:Internet/name_resolution"
Else
  Echo >DEVS:Internet/name_resolution "nameserver 192.168.50.30"
  Echo "Wrote DEVS:Internet/name_resolution (DNS 192.168.50.30)"
EndIf

Echo ""
Echo "Done. Reboot (or start your stack) - Roadshow will bring up"
Echo "scsidayna.device on 192.168.50.36. For troubleshooting set"
Echo "DEBUG=1 in ENVARC:scsidayna.prefs and re-copy it to ENV:."
